    ":question/math-academy-id": "e-1077",
    ":question/problem": "If $\\left(x^{-3}\\right)^{-6} = x^n,$ then what is $n?$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "We multiply the exponents, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\\left(x^{-3}\\right)^{-6}&=\\\n\tx^{(-3)(-6)}&=\\\n\tx^{18}\n\t}\n$$\n\nTherefore $n=18.$"
  },
