      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-2798",
      ":question/problem": "If ${({x}^{-3})}^{5}={x}^{k},$ then $k=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We multiply the exponents, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({x}^{-3})}^{5} & = \\\\ {x}^{(-3)5} & = \\\\ {x}^{-15}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $k=-15.$"
