      ":question/id": "b9bd1889-37e7-5c18-aff9-d79a4155a663",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-25388",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is equivalent to ${({p}^{0}{q}^{-3})}^{-3}?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we simplify the expression inside the parenthesis and then we apply the power rule\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({p}^{0}{q}^{-3})}^{-3} & = \\\\ {(1\\cdot {q}^{-3})}^{-3} & = \\\\ {({q}^{-3})}^{-3} & = \\\\ {q}^{(-3)(-3)} & = \\\\ {q}^{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    }
  ],
  ":knowledge-point/title": "Using the Power Rule with Negative Exponents"
